    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if they're basically just \"perpetually vulnerable\" unless they can gang up with others, doesn't that mean the whole idea of \"global governance\" is just a facade? it feels like the goal isn't really shared prosperity or peace, but just creating a way for the powerful to manage everyone else under a thin layer of legitimacy. would you say the push for more \"global integration\" is actually just a way to erode national sovereignty for the sake of a centralized authority?",
